# A lane that checks the turns laid out has to lay them out. testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime and testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime write checks into each turn in the walk (CheckProof, Box, StrictEq, HasArrayStorage,
# GetArrayLength), a turn that holds them is not laid out, and so every check of the emitters on what a front has found was text that never ran. Under testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly the walk writes nothing
# more: the same loops are laid out, in the same ways, as in an executable, and the checks stand in their turns.
# RUN: compile UnrolledLoopsEmitted UnrolledLoopsForMaskedIndexes UnrolledLoopsForTypedArrays UnrolledLoopStorageChecksHoisted UnrolledLoopTypeProofsChecked mechanisms=all
# CHECK: statistic UnrolledLoopsEmitted 65
# CHECK: statistic UnrolledLoopsForMaskedIndexes 5
# CHECK: statistic UnrolledLoopsForTypedArrays 5
# CHECK: statistic UnrolledLoopStorageChecksHoisted 21
# CHECK: statistic UnrolledLoopTypeProofsChecked 0
# RUN(LANE): compile UnrolledLoopsEmitted UnrolledLoopsForMaskedIndexes UnrolledLoopsForTypedArrays UnrolledLoopStorageChecksHoisted UnrolledLoopTypeProofsChecked mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly
# LANE: statistic UnrolledLoopsEmitted 65
# LANE: statistic UnrolledLoopsForMaskedIndexes 5
# LANE: statistic UnrolledLoopsForTypedArrays 5
# LANE: statistic UnrolledLoopStorageChecksHoisted 21
# LANE: statistic UnrolledLoopTypeProofsChecked 344
# RUN(PROOFS): compile UnrolledLoopsEmitted mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# PROOFS: statistic UnrolledLoopsEmitted 0
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly
# ANSWERS: 1834286507 1834286507 -1180011872 -1180011872 288 50
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
